---
import AdminLayout from '../../components/AdminLayout.astro';
import { mediaExtensionText } from '../../server/admin';

const ext = mediaExtensionText();
---
<AdminLayout title="Export guide" current="/admin/export-guide">
  <p>The importer reads photos, videos and audio, and the caption files that some download tools save next to them. Drop zips or folders on the Import page; everything else stays on your computer.</p>

  <h2>Plain files</h2>
  <p>Photos ({ext.image}), videos ({ext.video}) and audio ({ext.audio}). Each file becomes one post, dated by the file's date. You can add captions afterwards on the Posts page.</p>

  <h2>Videos and music saved with yt-dlp</h2>
  <p>Run yt-dlp with <code>--write-info-json</code> (and <code>--write-subs</code> for subtitles). The title, description, tags, upload date and original link come from the <code>.info.json</code> file next to each video, and <code>.vtt</code> or <code>.srt</code> files become subtitles.</p>

  <h2>Photo posts saved with gallery-dl</h2>
  <p>Run gallery-dl with <code>--write-metadata</code>. Files of the same post are grouped into one post in their original order, with the caption and date from the <code>.json</code> files.</p>

  <h2>Instagram and Facebook exports</h2>
  <p>The importer for the zips you download from Instagram or Facebook ("Download your information") arrives in a later update. Until then, an export like that is refused as a whole, and nothing in it is uploaded.</p>

  <h2>What is never uploaded</h2>
  <p>Messages, contacts, followers, login and security records, ads data, and anything else that is not a photo, video, audio file or its caption file. GPS positions are removed from photos and videos unless the site's configuration keeps them.</p>
</AdminLayout>
